   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Тимур, ты что тут наделал?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Timur, what have you done here?' The grammar packs 'Timur' and 'make' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Брат, ты только не переживай!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Brother, just do not worry!' In Russian, the idea of 'brother' flows naturally into 'to worry' without extra filler words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Я его не сильно сбил.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I did not hit him very hard.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'I' before landing on 'knock down'. the inspector answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Это просто ужасная гостиница!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is simply a terrible hotel!' The grammar packs 'this' and 'hotel' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Меня здесь все хотят убить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Everyone here wants to kill me.' The meaning hinges on 'me' working together with 'to kill' in spoken Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Чудо, что я остался жив.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It is a miracle that I stayed alive.' Notice how Russian expresses 'miracle' and 'alive' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Что вам от меня надо?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What do you want from me?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'what' before landing on 'need'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Предлагаю написать хороший отзыв.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I suggest writing a good review.' Notice how Russian expresses 'suggest' and 'review' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Вы намекаете мне на взятку?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Are you hinting at a bribe to me?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'you' before landing on 'bribe'. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Мы хотим возместить ваш ущерб.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We want to compensate your damage.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'we', while 'damage' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "inspector",
   "t": "Это просто очень возмутительно!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is simply very outrageous!' the inspector anchors the line on 'this', while 'outrageous' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Где я возьму такие деньги?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Where will I get that kind of money?' Notice how Russian expresses 'where' and 'money' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Хорошо, мы на всё согласны.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Fine, we agree to everything.' The meaning hinges on 'well' working together with 'agree' in spoken Russian. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
